window.WIKI_ENTRY={"id": "concept-037", "name_zh": "实相", "name_en": "reality", "tagline": "赛斯说的「实相」不是一个，你熟悉的物质世界只是其中一层「伪装」；梦、思想、情感和无数平行系统都同样是真的，而且你正在亲手形成你经验到的那一份。", "explanation": "赛斯说的「实相」不是一个，而是一整片层叠交错的存在。你熟悉的物质世界只是其中一层「伪装」——像幕布一样真实却挡住了更深的实相；梦、思想、情感都拥有各自独立、有效的实相，并不只是脑子里的幻想。你的五种感官只给你很窄的一束，内在感官和换一个意识焦点才能通向内在实相与无数平行、或然的系统。最关键的一句话是「你形成你自己的实相」：你的心理结构决定你感知到什么，信念像滤镜，而想像力正是你先在心里成形、再外在化实相的能力。多重实相并非互不相关——一切之中有一体性，所有系统在一个点融合，内我在「架构二」里的行动解释了架构一里许多看似不合理的巧合。实相既是私人的也是群体的：你的冲动汇成群体实相，而文化信念决定了哪些行为被算作「真实」。", "definitions": [{"zh": "实相之间有一种持续不断的交互切换，比如你们的物质建构世界与你们的意识感知不到的世界之间就是如此。", "en": "There is a constant interchange between the realities, such as your world of physical construction and the worlds of construction which you do not consciously perceive.", "source": "Session 66"}, {"zh": "你形成你自己的实相。", "en": "You form your own reality.", "source": "Session 812"}, {"zh": "在心灵的生命里，一个梦不论是否在醒时的生活中复现，都不使它更真或更不真。梦的事件发生在一个不相同的范围——你可说，是个想象的范围，因此，此刻你经验到一个自己独立存在有效的实相，在其中心灵自己的语言被给予了更大的自由。", "en": "In the life of the psyche a dream is no more or less “true,” whether or not it is duplicated in waking life. Dream events happen in a different context — one, you might say, of the imagination. Here you experience a valid reality that exists on its own, so to speak; one in which the psyche’s own language is given greater freedom.", "source": "Session 782"}, {"zh": "我们关切的实相，流经你们的伪装世界，形成你们用来建造建筑物的材料，也渗入你们世界的每一个原子和分子内，但它并不是源自你们的世界。", "en": "The reality with which we are concerned flows through your camouflage world, forms the material with which you build your constructions, permeates every atom and molecule in your world, but does not originate in your world.", "source": "Session 37"}], "blocks": [{"id": "B01", "title": "你以为的「现实」只是实相的一层", "note": "赛斯最先把人们口中的现实拆成两层：外层是你们用身体感官接触的物质世界，他称之为「伪装」层——不是假，而是像幕布一样挡住了更深的实相；内层是「内在实相」，秩序比伪装世界更多、对纪律的要求也更高，而不是更少。我们关切的那股实相像水一样流经你们的伪装世界、渗进每一个原子，却并不源自这个世界；你们织出自己的伪装存在就像蜘蛛织网，只是丝线是从你们自己里面生出来的，而且你们的建构可以在许多层面同时拥有实相。实相之间一直在互相切换、互相交融，物质建构的世界和你们意识感知不到的世界之间从不停歇；连各个系统外缘那些完全没有伪装的区域，也都遵循同一套设置。一个编号只属于一个块。", "src": "第 20、34、37、40、66、107、154、174、275、287 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 20 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 34 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 37 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 40 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 66 节"}, {"n": 6, "id": null, "label": "第 107 节"}, {"n": 7, "id": null, "label": "第 154 节"}, {"n": 8, "id": null, "label": "第 174 节"}, {"n": 9, "id": null, "label": "第 275 节"}, {"n": 10, "id": null, "label": "第 287 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-037-e0011", "zh": "内在感官从实相的内在世界传递资讯给身体。外在感官从伪装的外在世界传递资讯给身体。不过，内在感官一直在觉察身体自己的生理数据（physical data），而外在感官则主要关心身体与伪装环境的关系。换句话说，内在感官对身体有着直接又不变的认识，这是外在感官没有的。", "en": "The inner senses deliver data from the inner world of reality to the body. The outer senses deliver data from the outside world of camouflage to the body. However, the inner senses are aware of the body’s own physical data at all times, while the outer senses are concerned with the body mainly in its relationship to camouflage environment. In other words the inner senses have an immediate, constant knowledge of the body in a way that the outer senses do not.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第20节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "20", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-037-e0043", "zh": "其实，内在实相里的秩序，比你们的伪装世界更多，而且对纪律的要求更多，而不是更少。这样的药物实验会产生可怕的后果。伪装模式完全崩解，失序的人格无处立足，可能落入一种状态中，因失去了方向感而使你无法回到你的层次，同时忽视和缺乏纪律也会让你无法进入另一个层次。在这样的情况下，后果十分悲惨。", "en": "There is, if anything, more order in the inner reality than in your camouflage world, and more, not less discipline is required. Such drug experiments could have dire consequences. The camouflage pattern is completely broken up, the disorganized personality is afloat and could slip into a state where disorientation would prevent return to your level, while ignorance and lack of discipline prevented entry onto another level. The consequences would be completely disastrous in such a circumstance.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第34节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "34", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-037-e0053", "zh": "没有观念可以关在盒子里。我们关切的实相，流经你们的伪装世界，形成你们用来建造建筑物的材料，也渗入你们世界的每一个原子和分子内，但它并不是源自你们的世界。也就是说，它不是起源于你们的伪装世界。", "en": "No concepts can be boxed in. The reality with which we are concerned flows through your camouflage world, forms the material with which you build your constructions, permeates every atom and molecule in your world, but does not originate in your world. That is, it does not originate in your camouflage world.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第37节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "37", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-037-e0064", "zh": "你们建构你们的伪装存在，就如同蜘蛛织它的网一样，可是你们却不会觉察到丝线的奥秘。虽然卑微的蜘蛛编织着它的网子时，你们很容易会心一笑，但并不了解这些丝线是在你们自己里面产生的。蜘蛛的建构被严格地限定在一个层面，而你们的建构则不是，你们可能在许多层面立刻会有实相产生，产生的方式你们自己也不熟悉。", "en": "You construct your own camouflage existence as the spider constructs his web, but you are not aware of the threads. You do not understand that they originate within yourself, although it is very simple to smile as the lowly spider weaves its web. The spiders construction is severely limited to one plane, but this is not the case with your constructions, which may have reality on many planes at once, and in ways with which you are not familiar.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第40节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "40", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-037-e0137", "zh": "实相之间有一种持续不断的交互切换，比如你们的物质建构世界与你们的意识感知不到的世界之间就是如此。", "en": "There is a constant interchange between the realities, such as your world of physical construction and the worlds of construction which you do not consciously perceive.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第66节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "66", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-037-e0246", "zh": "在这些维度中，你们并不是以你们所是而被认识。你们不是以你们的人类形式而被认知。你们只是借由效应而被认识。在某些这类维度当中，你们在化学上，甚至在电子上是一个实相，在另外一些当中，你们在电磁上是一个实相。", "en": "You are not known for what you are in these dimensions. You are not recognized in your human form. You are known only by effects. In some of these dimensions you are chemically and even electrically a reality, in others electro-magnetically.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第107节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "107", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-037-e0431", "zh": "基于实际所需，你们的确必须假设，好像除了你们熟悉的实相之外，这辆车没有其他实相似的，但实情并非如此。我提过可以去感觉声音，因为这是潜藏在你们自己的肉体系统之内的一种能力，但是当不同系统的居民所感知到的实相，也存在于你们自己的系统之内，此时一般而言，这种感知资料的戏法一样会发生。", "en": "You must indeed for practical reasons pretend as if the automobile had no reality except the reality with which you are familiar, but this is not the case. I mentioned feeling sound because this is a capability that lies latent within your own physical system, but this same sort of a juggling of perspective data is what happens, generally speaking, when inhabitants of a different system perceive realities that also have an existence within your own system.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第154节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "154", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-037-e0517", "zh": "醒时状态与睡时状态两者间的相互关系，从来都未被清楚了解过。醒时与睡时状态的主要差异，仅仅是涉入的焦点完全改变。如果你只单独使用理性的方法，必然达不到任何梦实相研究的标准。人类真的就只知道用理性，但除了理性之外，人类还有更多。", "en": "The interrelationship between the waking state and the sleeping state has never been clearly understood. One of the main differences between the waking and sleeping states is merely the almost complete change of focus that is involved. When you are using intellectual methods alone you will necessarily fall short in any study of the dream reality. Man is indeed his intellect, but he is much else besides.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第174节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "174", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-037-e0826", "zh": "但是，这并不是说你不存在于明显的间隔（interval）之中。我们针对物质本质的讨论在这里很重要，因为我解释了发生在原子之中的脉动。当你试图检视独立存在于物质之外的实相时，你对时间的感知会造成很多困难。由于口语沟通的限制，有些很难解释。（例如，见第一册和第二册。）", "en": "This does not mean that you do not exist however in the apparent interval. Our discussion concerning the nature of matter is important here, for I explained the pulsations that occur in atoms. Your perception of time causes many difficulties when you try to examine reality as it exists independent of matter. The limitations of verbal communications make some explanations difficult. （See Volumes I and 2, for example.）", "source": "早期课第6册 · 第275节", "year": "1967", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第6册", "session": "275", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-037-e0863", "zh": "接着你会遇见伪装区域的中心。在各个不同的系统外缘有完全没有伪装的区域，这些区域应该会让你想起潜意识里各个不同生命周期之间没有分化的区域。这不是巧合，因为这个常规设置发生在所有的实相中。", "en": "You would then encounter the heart of the camouflage area. The completely uncamouflaged areas at the outer edges of the various systems should remind you of the undifferentiated areas between various life cycles in the subconscious. This is no coincidence, as this general setup occurs in all realities.", "source": "早期课第7册 · 第287节", "year": "1968", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第7册", "session": "287", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B02", "title": "你的感官只给你很窄的一束实相", "note": "外层感官是感知有限环境的绝佳工具，但人依赖它们太久，已经到了妨碍自己成长的地步；它们主要关心身体和伪装环境的关系，而内在感官从一开始就在觉察身体自己的生理数据，对身体的认识是外层感官没有的。意识心只不过是内我在某个时刻聚焦的方向，内我会不断改变它的焦点：当自我不把范围限制在伪装实相之内时，你才看得到梦的实相。思想有它自己的形状，只是外层感官看不见；情感则被电子编码，拥有独立的电子实相，它代表的恰恰是被建构成伪装之前那股没有伪装的宇宙生命力。在梦里熟悉的物理支柱会消失，内在的我照样运作得很好；但要操纵物质实相，内在的我需要一个适应物质状态的自己，那就是自我。大脑里那些没被用到的部分，本来就能以别的方式感知物质实相——你们这个物种本来也可以「闻声音、看颜色」。换个焦点，你甚至能同时觉知两个实相。", "src": "第 24、55、86、94、120、134、208、308、334、493 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 24 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 55 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 86 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 94 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 120 节"}, {"n": 6, "id": null, "label": "第 134 节"}, {"n": 7, "id": null, "label": "第 208 节"}, {"n": 8, "id": null, "label": "第 308 节"}, {"n": 9, "id": null, "label": "第 334 节"}, {"n": 10, "id": null, "label": "第 493 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-037-e0022", "zh": "心理时间让“持续时间”更久。你会发现在这里还有别的东西。从心理时间架构内，你会看到钟表时间和你一度以为的内在时间一样，如梦似幻、稍纵即逝。你会发现内在时间和你一度认为的外在时间一样真实。你会发现你的全我们（whole selves）在其他的世界里，同时向内和向外窥视，发现所有的时间都是同一个时间，所有的划分都是幻相。", "en": "Psychological time adds duration. You will find something else here. From the framework of psychological time you will see that clock time is as dreamlike and fleeting as you once thought inner time was. And you will discover that inner time is as much a reality as you once thought outer time was. You will discover your whole selves in other worlds, peeping inward and outward at the same time, and finding that all time is one time, and that all divisions are illusion.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第24节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "24", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-037-e0121", "zh": "这个设定在个别自己之上的主观限制，是它对外在感官的依赖放到它身上的，当作感知实相的一个方法。外在感官是感知有限环境的绝佳工具，然而，人类依赖它们太久了，在这样依赖成瘾的情况下，现在它们有妨碍他自己成长和发展的危险。", "en": "This arbitrary limitation set upon the individual self is put upon it by its reliance upon the outer senses, as a method of perceiving reality. The outer senses are excellent tools of perception for limited circumstances. However, man has relied upon them so long, and with such cringing dependence, that now they threaten to hamper his own growth and development.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第55节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "55", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-037-e0184", "zh": "这一端于是可以代表自己的延伸，向外朝着物质宇宙。这个延伸，正如我所说，理论上是无止尽的。内在实相的世界于是可以想像成存在于这根管子的另一端。同样的，管子的一端代表自己进入物质实相世界的延伸，所以这根管子的另一端也是代表自己的延伸，进入实相的内在世界。", "en": "This end would then represent the extension of the self outward toward the physical universe. This extension, as I have mentioned, is theoretically endless. The world of inner reality would then be imagined as existing at the other end of this tube. And in the same manner that one end of the tube would represent the extension of the self into the world of physical reality, then so too would the other end of this tube represent the extension of the self into the inner world of reality.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第86节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "86", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-037-e0215", "zh": "催眠是检视梦的一种方法。我们的方法或许是最好的一个。内我持续不断改变它的焦点。我说过意识只不过是内我在特定时间聚焦的方向而已。为了检视梦的实相，必须趁自我没有把它的范围单单限制在伪装实相之内的时候，改变内我的焦点，转到内我在其中移动的那些方向。", "en": "Hypnosis is one method of examining dreams. Our method is perhaps the best one. The inner self constantly changes its focus. I have said that consciousness is merely the direction in which the inner self focuses at any particular time. In order to examine the reality of dreams it is necessary to change the focus of the inner self to those directions in which the inner self moves, when the ego does not limit its scope to camouflage reality only.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第94节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "94", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-037-e0277", "zh": "不同种类的力量也被这些场域运用在你们的宇宙上。在彻底了解它之前，不可能产生真正的进步。人类依然和表面打交道，像他现在这样主要依赖外在自我的种种力量，而它的目的是和表面实相打交道。", "en": "Force of various kinds is also exerted by these fields upon your universe. Until it is thoroughly understood little real progress can be made. Mankind still deals with surfaces, depending mainly as he does upon the powers of the outer ego, whose purpose it is to deal only with surface reality.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第120节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "120", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-037-e0340", "zh": "情感也是经过电子编码的，也有一个独立的电子实相。在物质层次上，它们兼具化学与电子的性质。情感的效力和力道不应该被过于高估，因为它们只是以稍微带点色彩的形式，代表宇宙经过内我之际那没有伪装的生命力。所以，情感代表的是，在被建构成伪装之前的这股生命力。", "en": "Emotions also are electrically coded, and also have an independent electrical reality. On a physical level they are both chemical and electrical. The validity and strength of emotions cannot be overestimated, for they represent in only slightly tinged form the uncamouflaged vitality of the universe as it passes through the inner self. Emotions represent, therefore, this vitality before it has been constructed into camouflage.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第134节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "134", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-037-e0633", "zh": "但在梦的状态，熟悉的物质支柱有时会消失。没有它们，内在的我也可以运作得非常好。不过为了操纵一个物质实相，内在的我需要一个可以适应物质状态的自己；那就是自我。", "en": "Yet within the dream state the familiar physical props sometimes disappear. The inner I operates very well without them. In order to manipulate a physical reality however, the inner I needs a self that is acclimated to physical conditions; hence the ego.", "source": "早期课第5册 · 第208节", "year": "1966", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第5册", "session": "208", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-037-e0917", "zh": "一旦开启这些生理门户，路就比较好走了。松果体、脑垂体和丘脑在这里是重要的。之前提过的盐巴和甲状腺有一种关联。单单是肉体的大脑，没有使用过的部分，在它们的能力之内就有它，比方说，听见颜色、闻到声音；换句话说，这些部分的功能，主要是没有使用的部分，还包含让你能够以各种其他方式感知物质实相的功能。早在专门化的感觉器官被统一采用之前，这些未分化的部位就已经存在。", "en": "Once these physical pathways are opened, the way becomes easier. The pineal, pituitary, and thalamus are important here. The salt mentioned earlier has a connection with the thyroid. The physical brains alone, the unused portions, have it within their ability, for example, to hear color, to smell sound; in other words, these portions contain among other things functions, unused mainly, that would allow you to perceive physical reality in various other fashions. These undifferentiated areas existed first before the specialized senseapparatus was uniformly adopted. As a species you could just as easily have smelled color rather than viewed it, you see. These portions of the brain, once activated, then allow you to switch sense impressions from one sense mechanism to another, you see.", "source": "早期课第7册 · 第308节", "year": "1968", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第7册", "session": "308", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-037-e0971", "zh": "因为这种由内而外的投射是自动的，了解这方面涉及的过程，有莫大的好处。肉身的自己好像是（划线）对物质刺激起反应，事实上，它当然是在对自己的实相起反应，然后向外投射。", "en": "For this projection of inner into outer is automatic. Understanding the processes involved is of great benefit. The physical self seems(underlined) to react to physical stimuli. Actually, of course, it is reacting to its own reality, projected outward.", "source": "早期课第8册 · 第334节", "year": "1969", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第8册", "session": "334", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-037-e1361", "zh": "那是你们的损失。现在，有一个办法——即便你们身在身体活动中、甚至高强度的心智工作中——也能改变内在的聚焦，使你们同时觉知两个实相，同时又能在你们必须周旋的物质实相里应对自如。现在，你们去问你们的贝加[Bega]（苏马利语），因为我已经把信息交给了他，也吩咐他转告你们。我们且看他有多称职。我也想知道他对你们说了什么，因为我要看看他是如何传达我的建议的。", "en": "It is your loss. Now, there is a way—when you are involved in physical activity, and even intense mental work—to change the inner focus so that you are aware of two realities at once and can manipulate quite easily in the physical reality as you must. Now, you ask your Bega, for I have told him the message, and I have told him to tell you. We shall see how good he is. And I want to know what he tells you for I want to see how he is delivering my suggestions.", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第493节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "493", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B03", "title": "梦、思想、情感都是「真」的，不只是脑子里的幻想", "note": "赛斯一再强调：你们当成幻想的东西，往往另有其实相。一个念头无法在实验室里被观察到，却千真万确地存在，而且一个念头的实相比现今任何理论都更接近宇宙的特性。情感有独立的电子实相；梦里的创造能力是全方位的，人格先在梦实相里测试并练习自己创造的方法，再把那套方式搬到物质实相里。一个人在梦里遇见一场电磁风暴，会发现那风暴是他自己的一部分，不是破坏性的而是创造性的，是最简单基本的实相之一。梦的影像除了是想像的实相之外，也都有一个实相；梦宇宙里的那些实相可能是你创造的，却和你吃下的蛋糕、吞下的毒药一样真实。在看似醒着的梦里，你确实醒着，只是处在一个不同的实相架构里。评判现实的一般标准在这里完全不适用。在心灵的生命里，一个梦不论是否在醒时复现，都不使它更真或更不真——它发生在一个不同的范围里，是一个独立存在、有效的实相，而且在这个范围里梦的「真实感」反而更真切。", "src": "第 44、78、128、183、199、232、259、265、269、782、786 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 44 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 78 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 128 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 183 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 199 节"}, {"n": 6, "id": null, "label": "第 232 节"}, {"n": 7, "id": null, "label": "第 259 节"}, {"n": 8, "id": null, "label": "第 265 节"}, {"n": 9, "id": null, "label": "第 269 节"}, {"n": 10, "id": null, "label": "第 782 节"}, {"n": 11, "id": null, "label": "第 786 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-037-e0090", "zh": "你们所认为的死亡，拥有的基本实相，并不比你们的时空概念来得大。死亡，其实代表你当下感知能量的转化、甚至价值完成能力之中的一个盲点。死亡，仅仅代表你自身感知的终止，也就是说，你的理解终止。你们这方面的能力等同于理解一种完全的缩减。你的感官并非配备来感知能量是从一个转化成另一个。", "en": "What you consider death has no more basic reality than has your idea of time and space. Death really represents a blind spot in your present ability to perceive energy transformation, and even value fulfillment. Death merely represents the termination of your own perception, that is, the termination of your understanding. Your ability here amounts to a complete dwindling of comprehension. Your senses are not equipped to perceive the transformation of energy from one form to another.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第44节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "44", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-037-e0168", "zh": "一个念头无法在你们任何实验室中以科学方式被观察到，但它千真万确地存在。一个念头不可能是一个封闭系统，但一个念头的实相，它的发展与潜能比起现今任何一个理论，都要更接近宇宙特性。", "en": "An idea, that cannot be scientifically observed in any of your laboratories, definitely exists. An idea is hardly a closed system, but the reality of an idea, its growth and potential, comes much closer to a description of the characteristics of the universe than any current theory.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第78节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "78", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-037-e0309", "zh": "就强度质量而言，思想是有形状的，但是你们看不见它们的形状；你们的外在感官没有感知到它。你们在你们自己之内某种程度看见梦的各种形状。你们没有看见梦本身，因为即使是这里，在赋予一个梦实相电子存在之后，你们还是必须拆解它，让它变得更简单，才能感知你们其实已经创造的东西。", "en": "Thoughts have shape in terms of intensity mass, though you cannot see their shape; your outer senses do not perceive it. You see within yourself the various shapes of dreams to a certain extent. You do not see the dream itself, for even here, after giving a dream reality, electrical existence, you must break it down into simpler terms so that you can perceive what you have indeed created.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第128节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "128", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-037-e0546", "zh": "创造的能力在梦境中主宰一切，人格最初就是在这里测试自己创造的强度和方法。因此，梦的存在大幅渲染和形成了人格的物质环境。有某种醒时生活的经验会渗漏到梦经验，不过这种渗漏往往代表了所需要的物质，或是有待解决的问题。精神事件和梦事件才是最原始的，个体刚开始都先在实相中操纵环境，然后再转移到物质实相中，以自己特有的方式操纵它们。", "en": "The creative abilities have full reign within the dream state, and it is here that the personality first tests its creative intensities and methods. The personality’s physical environment therefore is greatly colored and formed by his dream existence. There is some leakage from waking-life experience to dream experience, but this leakage usually represents the material needed, or the problem to be solved. Mental events and dream events are primary. The individual first manipulates situations within the dream reality, and then transposes his characteristic method of handling them upon the physical reality.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第183节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "183", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-037-e0604", "zh": "在梦中，他走进自己的房间，发现他的能力和他的呼吸一样同为他的一部分，他不能随意地像开关收音机一样地把它关掉。他站在房间，有梦里有一个电磁性的风暴，房间里充满了跳动的电磁波。他很害怕。不过他了解他是这个风暴的一部分，这个风暴也是他自己的一部分，这不是破坏性而是创造性的；最重要的，这是一个实相简单基本的部分。", "en": "In the dream itself, he goes into his room and discovers that his ability is as much a part of him as his breath, and that he cannot turn it off and on at will, or turn it off as one would a radio. He stands in the room, and there is an electric storm in the dream, and the room is touched by vibrating currents. He is afraid. Nevertheless he realizes that he is part of the storm, and the storm is part of himself, and it is not destructive but creative; and most of all, a simple elemental part of reality as it is.", "source": "早期课第5册 · 第199节", "year": "1966", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第5册", "session": "199", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-037-e0692", "zh": "你只是没有聚焦在它上面，或者说，你的注意力没有聚焦在它上面。当你在做梦时，有时候你会觉知到它。我曾告诉过你们，这些印象除了是一个想像的实相，它们也都有一个实相。", "en": "You simply are not focused within it, or your attention is not focused within it. You sometimes become aware of it when you are in the dream state. Now I have told you that these images have a reality, beside an imaginative reality.", "source": "早期课第5册 · 第232节", "year": "1966", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第5册", "session": "232", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-037-e0766", "zh": "你处于这个发展的早期阶段，但它会来的。在梦宇宙之内的这些实相可能是你创造的，但它们和你吃的蛋糕，或你可能吞下的毒药一样真实。就像你的常识在物质宇宙中保护着你一样，在你进行梦物件的操纵时，也必须慎重斟酌。", "en": "You are at the early stages of this development, but it will come. These realities within the dream universe may be created by you, but they are as actual as the piece of cake that you eat, or the poison that you may swallow. As your common sense protects you in the physical universe, so you must use discretion as you progress into the manipulation of dream objects.", "source": "早期课第6册 · 第259节", "year": "1967", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第6册", "session": "259", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-037-e0786", "zh": "无论如何，你据以判断实相的一般标准在这里不适用，我再怎么强调这一点都不为过。约瑟，你必须学习新的规则。我们角落里的小朋友（珍指着安·黛伯乐）必须学习新的规则。现在。你遇到的每一个意象，以及每一次经验，在它自己的架构之内都各有不同。而且不要忘记，你遭遇到的经验对你自己的人格会产生影响，和任何醒时经验的影响一样强烈，或比它们更为强烈。", "en": "I cannot emphasize too strongly however the fact that the ordinary standards by which you judge reality will not here apply. And Joseph, you must learn the new rules. Our small friend in the corner （Jane pointed to Ann Diebler） must learn the new rules. Now. Every image that you meet, and every experience, will be varied within its own framework. And do not forget that the experiences which you encounter will have an effect upon your own personality, as vivid or more vivid than the effect of any waking experience.", "source": "早期课第6册 · 第265节", "year": "1967", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第6册", "session": "265", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-037-e0806", "zh": "你明白，你可以使用批判能力。但是你看，当你这样做的时候，你晓得你就不是在平常的醒时状态。在看似醒着的梦中，你确实是醒着的，当然是在一个不同的心理架构之内。甚至，是在一个不同的实相架构之内。", "en": "As you realize, you can use the critical faculties. But you see when you do so you realize that you are not in your normal waking condition. In awake-seeming dreams you are indeed awake, within of course a different psychological framework. Indeed, within a different framework of reality.", "source": "早期课第6册 · 第269节", "year": "1967", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第6册", "session": "269", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-037-e3217", "zh": "在心灵的生命里，一个梦不论是否在醒时的生活中复现，都不使它更真或更不真。梦的事件发生在一个不相同的范围——你可说，是个想象的范围，因此，此刻你经验到一个自己独立存在有效的实相，在其中心灵自己的语言被给予了更大的自由。", "en": "In the life of the psyche a dream is no more or less “true,” whether or not it is duplicated in waking life. Dream events happen in a different context — one, you might say, of the imagination. Here you experience a valid reality that exists on its own, so to speak; one in which the psyche’s own language is given greater freedom.", "source": "心灵的本质 · 第782节", "year": "1975–77", "tag": null, "short": "心灵的本质", "session": "782", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-037-e3249", "zh": "你生活中的每件事，都是包含在另外每件事里的。同样的，每一生都包含在另外的每一生之中。那么，在梦境，对实相的感觉是「更真切的」。在某范围内，你能对梦变得更有意识地觉察——亦即是有意识地觉察你做梦的过程。那也能容许你「做梦的自己」在醒时状态有更多的表现。借着多半与创造力相连的技术可以连成此点。", "en": "Each event of your life is contained within each other event. In the same way, each lifetime is contained in each other lifetime. The feeling of reality is “truer” then in the dream state. You can become consciously aware of your dreams to some extent — that is, consciously aware of your own dreaming. You can also allow your “dream self” greater expression in the waking state. This can be done through techniques that are largely connected with creativity.", "source": "心灵的本质 · 第786节", "year": "1975–77", "tag": null, "short": "心灵的本质", "session": "786", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B04", "title": "你正在形成你自己的实相", "note": "这是赛斯最常被引用的一句话：你形成你自己的实相。他给过一幅图：你们的醒时实相像一出电视剧，戏是你自己创造的，你借着身体这个「接收器」调到一大片节目区里，而那里有许多不同的「电视台」都活了过来——你既是戏，也是看戏的人。决定你能感知到什么的关键，是你自己的心理结构：环境不是独立在外的东西，它是知觉方式的结果，而知觉方式由心理结构决定。自我几乎可以把意识心完全当成一种工具，只去感知符合它既有信念的实相。所以检视并理解自己的信念极为重要——旧的实相有它的黏着力，新的也同样有。你想要的那些能力其实已经是潜在的，如果你明白可能性的本质，就不需要假装忽略现状，而能把它认作你已经具体化的一个可能实相，再启动把不同可能性带进实质经验的过程。想像力最初正是把你们和其他动物分开的东西，它让你们先在心里形成实相，再「后来」把它外在化。反过来，若你觉得自己是命运的卒子、在造成自己的实相里完全没参一手，你就永远会是个受害者。", "src": "第 511、515、616、622、656、669、742、756、812、894 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 511 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 515 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 616 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 622 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 656 节"}, {"n": 6, "id": null, "label": "第 669 节"}, {"n": 7, "id": null, "label": "第 742 节"}, {"n": 8, "id": null, "label": "第 756 节"}, {"n": 9, "id": null, "label": "第 812 节"}, {"n": 10, "id": null, "label": "第 894 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-037-e1444", "zh": "我对那些信神与不信神的人讲话，对那些相信科学会找到有关实相性质的所有答案，或不相信的人讲话。我希望给你们线索，使你们能够前所未有地亲自研究实相的性质。", "en": "I speak to those who believe in a god, and those who do not, to those who believe that science will find all answers as to the nature of reality, and to those who do not. I hope to give you clues that will enable you to study the nature of reality for yourself as you have never studied it before.", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第511节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "511", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-037-e1948", "zh": "由于你们心理结构的原故使得你们的物质环境呈现出你们今天所见到的外貌。如果你们转而以“观念的联想过程”来感觉自己生命的延续，而不用“自己在时间中过来多少日子”来感觉自己持续的存在，那么你们便可以以一种崭新的角度来感受这个物质世界，你们可以在瞬间认识各种过去现在的事物，并可在事物所显示的各种现象中举一反三。假设：你父亲一生中有八张心爱的椅子，如果你用“领悟后的联想”来当作知觉的工具，而不用时间先后秩序来感觉，那么你能在一瞬间就晓得所有的八张椅子，甚至是只要看到一张便能知道其他的。所以环境不是一个独立于外的东西，它是知觉方式的结果，知觉方式有心灵结构来决定。", "en": "Your own physical environment appears as it does to you because of your own psychological structure. If you gained your sense of personal continuity through associative processes primarily, rather than as a result of the familiarity of self moving through time, then you would experience physical reality in an entirely different fashion. Objects from past and present could be perceived at once, their presence justified through associative connections. Say that your father throughout his lifetime has eight favorite chairs. If your perceptive mechanisms were primarily set up as a result of intuitive association rather than time sequence, then you would perceive all of these chairs at one time; or seeing one, you would be aware of the others. So environment is not a separate thing in itself, but the result of perceptive patterns, and these are determined by psychological structure.", "source": "时空之外 · 第515节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "时空之外", "session": "515", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-037-e2014", "zh": "在意识心的活动里，有各种等级和波动起伏。它的弹性远大过于你的认定。（停顿。）自我几乎可以完全把意识心当做感知符合其信念的外在或内在实相的一种方法。因此，问题不是出在某些答案没有公然任人取用，而是出在，你常常把自己设定在一个你相信的行动方向上，任何可能与你当前信念有所冲突的资料，你都不想要开放自己去接纳。", "en": "There are gradations and fluctuations within its activity. It is far more flexible than you give it credit for. (Pause.) The ego can use the conscious mind almost entirely as a way of perceiving external or internal realities that coincide with its own beliefs. It is not that certain answers do not lie openly accessible, therefore, but that often you have set yourself on a course of action in which you believe, and you do not want to open yourself to any material that may contradict your current beliefs.", "source": "个人实相的本质 · 第616节", "year": "1972–73", "tag": null, "short": "个人实相的本质", "session": "616", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-037-e2066", "zh": "你可能在那方面变得越来越有效率。这就是为什么我说，为你自己检视信念，并且了解它对你有什么个人的意义，是极为重要的事。再用那个例子来讲，如果你突然开始明白了你的地位，开始直接对孩子表达你的爱，也许你会发现他们相当惊讶，十分髙兴却又很困惑。可能要过一阵子他们才能了解你的行为，但正如旧的实相有种黏着力，新的也一样有。", "en": "You may become more and more efficient in that manner. This is why it is vital that you examine your beliefs for yourself and understand what they mean to you personally. If, using that example, you suddenly begin to realize your position and begin to express your love to your children directly, you may find them quite surprised, delighted but confused. It may take them a while to understand your reactions, but as the old reality had a cohesiveness so will the new.", "source": "个人实相的本质 · 第622节", "year": "1972–73", "tag": null, "short": "个人实相的本质", "session": "622", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-037-e2222", "zh": "以你们的话来说，你也许想要实现的能力、力量等，已经是潜在的，并可为你所用。假设你不健康而希望自己健康，如果你了解可能性的本质，就不需要假装去忽视你目前的情况。反之，你将了悟它是你已将之具体化的一个可能实相，认清事实之后，你就可以开始那个把不同可能性带入实质经验所需要的过程。", "en": "The abilities, strengths and variants that you may want to actualize are already latent, in your terms, and at your disposal. Suppose that you are unhealthy and desire health. If you understand the nature of probabilities, you will not need to pretend to ignore your present situation. You will recognize it instead as a probable reality that you have physically materialized. Taking that for granted, you will then begin the process necessary to bring a different probability into physical experience.", "source": "个人实相的本质 · 第656节", "year": "1972–73", "tag": null, "short": "个人实相的本质", "session": "656", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-037-e2274", "zh": "你常常不信任自己的想象力，而认为它是在处理一种不能被称为事实的现象。因此，你人工地来形成一个情况，在其中，你必须画出整个图形。例如，如果你太有想象力，也许不能适当地处理实质生活。然而，这只适用于你目前运作的文化媒介里。以你们的时间来讲，最初正是那个想象力以自己的方式把你们与其他动物分开，而使你们能在自己心中形成“后来”可将之外在化的实相。", "en": "Often you do not trust your imagination, considering that it deals with phenomena that cannot be called fact. Therefore you artificially form a situation in which overall traces must be made. If you are too imaginative, for example, you may not be able to adequately deal with physical life. This applies only in the cultural media in which you presently operate, however. Originally, and in your terms of time, it was precisely the imagination that in its own way set you apart from other creatures, enabling you to form realities in your mind that you could “later” exteriorize.", "source": "个人实相的本质 · 第669节", "year": "1972–73", "tag": null, "short": "个人实相的本质", "session": "669", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-037-e2972", "zh": "那么，你觉得好像你是命运的卒子，而可能行动的概念看起来像是最全然的废话。每个事件看起来都是不可避免的，如果这心态被过度强调的话，那么，甚至会像是你在造成你自己的实相里完全没有参一手的样子，而你会永远觉得自己是一个受害者。", "en": "Then you feel as if you are the pawns of fate, and the idea of probable actions seems like the sheerest nonsense. Each event seems inevitable. If this attitude is carried to excessive lengths, then it even appears that you have no hand at all in the making of your own reality. You will always feel yourself a victim.", "source": "未知的实相卷二 · 第742节", "year": "1974–75", "tag": null, "short": "未知的实相卷二", "session": "742", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-037-e3153", "zh": "你们正常的醒时实相可以被比喻为一种电视剧，在其中你直接参与所有演出的戏。本来就是你创造了他们。你们形成了你们个人的与共同的探险，而借由一个特殊的方式运用你自己的实相工具——你的身体——你把他们带入了你的经验，你对着一个大的节目安排区调整频率，可是那儿有许多不同的电视台（in a particular way， tuned in to a large programming area in which， however， there are many different stations.）。在你们来说，这些电视台变成了活的。你就是你体验的戏剧。而所有的活的似乎都围着你转。你也是那收看的人。", "en": "Now: Your normal waking reality can be compared to a kind of television drama in which you participate directly in all of the dramas presented. You create them to begin with. You form your private and joint adventures, and bring them into experience by using your physical apparatus — your body — in a particular way, tuned in to a large programming area in which, however, there are many different stations. In your terms, these stations come alive. You are the drama that you experience, and all of your activities seem to revolve about you. You are also the perceiver.", "source": "心灵的本质 · 第756节", "year": "1975–77", "tag": null, "short": "心灵的本质", "session": "756", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-037-e3370", "zh": "你形成你自己的实相。然而，如果你冬天是在美国的西北部，那么你最好还是经验到一个具体的冬天（幽默的），否则，你就与主要的感官资料距离得太远了。", "en": "You form your own reality. Yet if you are in the Northeast in the wintertime, you had better be experiencing a physical winter (humorously), or you are far divorced from primary sense data.", "source": "个人与群体事件的本质 · 第812节", "year": "1977–79", "tag": null, "short": "个人与群体事件的本质", "session": "812", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-037-e3585", "zh": "我所能想到的最好的比喻是，直到那时，自己是像一个心理的橡皮筋，以极大的力量与活力向内向外弹，但却没有任何一种够僵化的心理架构来维持一个身体的姿势。内我仍然与梦实相保持关系，同时，身体的取向，以及身体的意识，获得一种伟大的身体冒险、好奇及惊奇感——如本来计划的——因此，再度的，内我将其意识的一部分放在一个不同的包装里。如它一度形成了身体意识，现在它形成了一个向身体调准的意识，一个自己，其欲望和意图的取向是内我无法单独做到的。", "en": "(Pause at 9:42.) Give us a moment…. The best analogy I can think of is that up to that time the self was like a psychological rubber band, snapping inward and outward with great force and vitality, but without any kind of rigid-enough psychological framework to maintain a physical stance. The inner self still related to dream reality, while the body’s orientation and the body consciousness attained, as was intended, a great sense of physical adventure, curiosity, speculation, wonder—and so once again the inner self put a portion of its consciousness in a different parcel, so to speak. As once it had formed the body consciousness, now it formed a physically attuned consciousness, a self whose desires and intents would be oriented in a way that, alone, the inner self could not be.", "source": "梦、进化与价值完成 · 第894节", "year": "1979–82", "tag": null, "short": "梦、进化与价值完成", "session": "894", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B05", "title": "平行实相、或然实相与其他系统", "note": "你们以为同时同空间存在的只有自己这一个地球，但平行存在一直在发生：那些持续被组织化、具体化的实相有自己的文化、历史、伪装模式和扭曲，也有在你们看来是个体的生物。实相的可能性是无止境的，你熟悉的那一小部分，是你此刻的感知特质替你划定的。连一场溃疡都在许多层面拥有实相，必须从类似的角度处理。两种状态（醒与睡）之间确实有连结，而且有确定的实相同时存在于两种状态里——找到这些「联合的实相」才能看清人格运作的实相本质。人死后人格会逐渐进入下一个实相，在下一个系统里汇集能量；系统本身是实相展现自己的方式，而无论方法怎么变，实相都有某些属于它自己的特征，每个实相存在于独一无二的坐标里，主要焦点完全独特。除了物质世界，你们每一位同时还存在于非物质的世界里；你们的每个轻微思想和情感，都会以许多你们这个领域之外的方式显现。在梦里你们认识可能事件并从中选择——广义说来，生与死都是你选的。意识单位同时形成所有的系统，细胞结构知道它自己不被身体束缚。", "src": "第 29、43、141、161、211、398、406、409、560、681、688 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 29 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 43 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 141 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 161 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 211 节"}, {"n": 6, "id": null, "label": "第 398 节"}, {"n": 7, "id": null, "label": "第 406 节"}, {"n": 8, "id": null, "label": "第 409 节"}, {"n": 9, "id": null, "label": "第 560 节"}, {"n": 10, "id": null, "label": "第 681 节"}, {"n": 11, "id": null, "label": "第 688 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-037-e0032", "zh": "你们当然感知不到这些你们会说同时和你们存在同样空间的其他层面，但是平行存在却一直在发生中。组织化，具体化的各种持续实相正在发生，有它们自己的文化、历史、理论、伪装模式和扭曲，同时，它们自己也有在你们看来是个体的生物。", "en": "These other planes that you would say exist simultaneously with you in the same space as your earth, are unperceived of course by you. Parallel existences occur constantly. Continual organized materialization realities are happening with their own cultures, histories, theories, camouflage patterns and distortions, with their own beings existing as individuals in your terms.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第29节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "29", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-037-e0075", "zh": "如果可以的话，想像在这个空间指定的固定范围内，画中的人物或居民有其心理实相。换句话说，想像意识、生长、实相和扩展，与你们所说的空间扩展无关，而是在心理实相上拥有几乎完全的自由，那么你至少会有点了解我说一个扩展中的宇宙，它和你们科学家讲的扩展中的宇宙毫不相干是什么意思。", "en": "Imagine if you can the figures or inhabitants in the painting having psychological reality, all within the set limits prescribed by the given space. Imagine in other words consciousness, growth, reality and expansion, having nothing to do with expansion of space in your terms, but an almost complete freedom of psychological realities, and you will come at least within the realm of understanding what I mean by an expanding universe that has nothing to do with the expanding universe of which your scientists speak.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第43节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "43", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-037-e0371", "zh": "行动，你可以说，被它自己席卷而去。实相的可能性是无止境的。你熟悉的实相是非常小的部分。你的感知特质这时候，指定限制你可以感知的行动面向。不过，你可以非常清楚地聚焦在其他面向上。而且特定的意识类型和本体只不过是行动形成感知模式导致的结果，它透过这些模式，得以聚焦在某些自己的面向上。", "en": "Action, you may say, is carried away by itself. Reality possibilities are endless. You are familiar with very small portions of reality. Your perception characteristics at this time dictate and limit the aspects of action that you can perceive. You can, however, focus very clearly on other aspects. And particular types of consciousness and identities are merely the result of action’s formation into perception patterns with which it can focus upon certain aspects of itself.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第141节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "141", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-037-e0460", "zh": "还有一点，以溃疡为例，这个病有许多层面的实相，都必须以类似的方式处理，即使从目前这个自我的观点来看，尚不足以处理；因为这实际上牵涉到一些原因，而目前的自我必定大都不太清楚。不过在内我的指挥下，有其全部的论据和全部的原因。", "en": "One more point. The ulcer for example has reality upon many levels, and must be dealt with in a like manner, for it is not enough to handle it even from the viewpoint of the present ego; for indeed causes are involved of which the present ego must necessarily be mainly ignorant. The inner self however has at its command all these reasoning’s, and all these causes.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第161节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "161", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-037-e0648", "zh": "现在在两种状态之间一定有连结。有明确的实相存在于两种状态下，而这个联合的实相就是你要寻找的。只有找到这些，你才能发现人类人格和其运作的实相本质。", "en": "Now there are indeed connections between these two conditions. And there are definite realities that exist in both states, and these uniting realities will be what you are looking for. For only by finding these can you discover the nature of the human personality and the nature of reality within which it must operate.", "source": "早期课第5册 · 第211节", "year": "1966", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第5册", "session": "211", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-037-e1049", "zh": "人格在身体的有机体内越来越不明显，人格本身并没有瓦解，由于各种原因，对有机体的控制已经减弱。在这些情况下，人格逐渐进入到下一个实相，在下一个系统中汇集能量。", "en": "The personality is less and less apparent within the physical organism. The personality itself has not disintegrated. Its control over the organism, for various reasons, has lessened. In these cases the personality gradually makes inroads into the next reality. It gathers its energy within the next system.", "source": "早期课第8册 · 第398节", "year": "1969", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第8册", "session": "398", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-037-e1075", "zh": "这些方式本身会有所变化。系统会变化，系统是实相的体现，因为实相会以各种形式展现自己，实相用来展现的方式本身也会变化。但是无论各种方法和各种不同的表现如何，实相都具有某些特征。", "en": "These methods themselves will vary. The systems vary, the systems being the manifestation of reality as it shows itself in various forms. The methods by which it manifests itself also vary. Certain characteristics however belong to reality regardless of the very methods and the various manifestations.", "source": "早期课第8册 · 第406节", "year": "1969", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第8册", "session": "406", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-037-e1101", "zh": "我们会努力向你解释坐标，我们才刚刚开始提示它们的实相和重要性。每个实相都存在于独一无二的坐标里面，会有一些重叠，但是任何系统内的主要焦点，都是完全独特，这没有矛盾，也没有例外，这适用在最微小的环境中。（停顿）任何经验都与其他经验有所不同，任何个体、任何自我结构也都是如此。", "en": "We will be working to explain coordinates to you. We are barely beginning to hint at their reality and importance. Every reality exists within unique coordinates. There is some overlapping, but the main focus within any system is entirely unique. There is no contradiction, no exception. This applies in the most minute circumstance. (Pause.) No experience is ever like any other, no individual or no self structure.", "source": "早期课第8册 · 第409节", "year": "1969", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第8册", "session": "409", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-037-e1957", "zh": "有许多的或然世界是以物质为主的，不过这种物质的或然系统只代表了整个或然系统的小小部分。你们每一位除了存在于物质世界里之外，还都同时存在于非物质的世界中。", "en": "There are many probable systems of reality, therefore, in which physical data predominates, but such physical probabilities represent but one small portion. Each of you also exist in nonphysical systems, and I have explained earlier that your slightest thought or emotion is manifested in many other ways than in your own field of existence.", "source": "时空之外 · 第560节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "时空之外", "session": "560", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-037-e2365", "zh": "在梦里，你知悉可能事件，而后你从中选择；（对我：）所以，当你作为一个孩子而死了之前，你知道你可以选择那死亡。广义说来，你选择生与死二者，而你那张十六岁时的照片在那个实相里根本没有拍。", "en": "In dreams you are acquainted with probable events, from which you then choose; (to me:) so before you died as a child, you knew that you could pick or choose that death. In greater terms you chose both life and death, and the picture of you at the age of 169 was never taken in one reality.", "source": "未知的实相卷一 · 第681节", "year": "1974–75", "tag": null, "short": "未知的实相卷一", "session": "681", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-037-e2443", "zh": "意识单位（CU’s）同时地形成所有的系统。在形成了你们的系统，而且由它们的能量把自己多样化成物质形式之后，它们是觉察到任何既定的生物类别之所有可能变奏的。从未有过任何直线的发展，如好比说，从爬虫到哺乳类、猿猴及人。反之，有生命形态及模式之了不起的、仍在继续的、无限丰富的平行爆发在尽可能多的方向里。以你们的话说，曾有分享时间与空间两者达数世纪之久的“动物—人”及“人—动物”。如你们全都十分明白的，这是一个在时间里的物质系统，此地，细胞死去而被取代，在细胞内的意识单位知道它们自己的不可摧毁性，只改变了形式，却维持住它们所曾是的所有细胞的身份。（热切的：）虽然细胞实质的死去，但其不可侵犯的本质并没有被出卖，它只不过不再是物质性的。", "en": "That kind of “death” is, then, natural in one way or another within your system. I will be speaking here from many viewpoints, and later I will discuss in full your ideas of mortality. Here, however, let me state that all life is cooperative. It also knows it exists beyond its form. The experience of your species involves a certain kind of consciousness development, highly vital. (Pause.) This necessitated a certain kind of specialization, a certain “long-term” identification with form. Cellular structure maintains brilliant effectiveness in the body’s present reality, but knows itself free of it. Man’s particular kind of consciousness fiercely identified with the body. This was a necessity to focus energy toward physical manipulation. To some important extent the same applies to the animals. The cell might gladly “die,” but the specifically oriented man-and-animal consciousness would not so willingly let go.", "source": "未知的实相卷一 · 第688节", "year": "1974–75", "tag": null, "short": "未知的实相卷一", "session": "688", "only_en": true}]}]}, {"id": "B06", "title": "多重实相怎么交融：一体、框架与坐标", "note": "尽管实相多到无穷，它们并非互不相关。一切之中有一体性：有一个点，所有次元和所有实相系统都在那里融合，意识也是如此——你是更大自己（一个存有）的一部分，所以你里面有一部分能通达那个存有的知识。早先的信仰比后来「督神」的信仰更好地代表了内在实相：那时人观察自然，让自然说话。你们当下的宇宙可以比作一个被群体共享的梦，它有效、有意义、建立在自发性的秩序上，只是从一个特定角度呈现实相；要理解它，你得走到意识的另一个层面，从那里反而看得更清楚。你意识里某一部分创造的那种实相是有效且真的，你换焦点去「旅行」，一点也不比从一座城市去另一座城市更虚；而你的单线式意识只是许多种「语言」之一，其他的一样天生、一样自然。当一切万有想到一个物质系统，它就被看不见地创造了，注定会浮现成物质实相。当你用上所有的心智，你才会比现在更清楚地感知实相、也更直接地理解它的本质。你们的心理实相隐含在我的实相之内，我的隐含在你们的之内，就像你们的实相隐含在猫的实相之内。内我的推理不受因果限制，它在「架构二」较广范围内的行动，解释了你们世界里许多看似不合理的巧合——架构二里的许多实相无法在架构一里被当作事实解释，常以艺术的象征语言出现，你们的许多梦就是这种转译。", "src": "第 448、587、700、713、723、744、763、790、823、827 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 448 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 587 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 700 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 713 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 723 节"}, {"n": 6, "id": null, "label": "第 744 节"}, {"n": 7, "id": null, "label": "第 763 节"}, {"n": 8, "id": null, "label": "第 790 节"}, {"n": 9, "id": null, "label": "第 823 节"}, {"n": 10, "id": null, "label": "第 827 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-037-e1236", "zh": "你们能凭直觉在某种程度上觉察到自己的历次转世，从而感到一种辨认得出的熟悉感。现在，万有之中有一体性。你们被告知，有一个点，一切次元与一切实相系统都在那里融合。意识也是如此。你们是一个更大自己——一个存有——的一部分；正因如此，你们之中便有一部分能够通达你们那个存有的知识。", "en": "You can intuitively become aware to some extent of your own reincarnations, so that you feel a recognizable sense of familiarity. Now there is unity in all. You have been told that there is a point where all dimensions and systems of reality merge. Now the same is true of consciousness. You are a part of a larger self, an entity, and because you are there is a portion of you that has access to the knowledge of your entity.", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第448节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "448", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-037-e1876", "zh": "希伯来人构想了一个督导神，一个愤怒、公正而有时残酷的神；于是，许多支派否认除了人之外其他的生物还拥有内在灵性的概念。早先的信仰则为内在实相的一个好得多的代表，在其中，人观察自然，让自然说话而透露它的秘密。", "en": "The Hebrews conceived of an overseer god, an angry and just and sometimes cruel god; and many sects denied, then, the idea that other living beings beside man possessed inner spirits. The earlier beliefs represented a far better representation of inner reality, in which man, observing nature, let nature speak and reveal its secrets.", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第587节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "587", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-037-e2520", "zh": "只当作一个比喻，让我们这么来看：你们现在的宇宙是一个为群体共享的梦，颇具有效性——以某种角度来表现实相的一个梦；这个梦最重要的是，它是有意义的、具创造性的，而且，并非建立在混乱上（以一个会心的眼色），却是建立在自发性的秩序上。可是，若要了解它，你必须去到意识的另一个层面——在那儿，也许，梦暂时的看来仿佛不那么的真实似的。从另外一个角度，在那儿，你甚至可以更清楚的看它，把它当作你手中的一张照片一样，同时，你也可由那更广的视角看到，你也的确是站在梦的范畴之外，但却又是在另一个“里面”里，而因为照片本身的限制，那是无法在照片里显出来的。", "en": "Simply as an analogy, look at it this way: Your present universe is a mass-shared dream, quite valid — a dream that presents reality in a certain light; a dream that is above all meaningful, creative, based not upon chaos (with a knowing look), but upon spontaneous order. To understand it, however, you must go to another level of consciousness — one where, perhaps, the dream momentarily does not seem so real. There, from another viewpoint, you can see it even more clearly, holding it like a photograph in your hands; at the same time you can see from that broader perspective that you do indeed also stand outside of the dream context, but in a “within” that cannot show in the snapshot because of its limitations.", "source": "未知的实相卷一 · 第700节", "year": "1974–75", "tag": null, "short": "未知的实相卷一", "session": "700", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-037-e2672", "zh": "我们正试着在两个层面上作比喻，所以请忍耐一下。就你们的心灵而言，你们自己的每一个思想与行为不只以你们熟悉的方式存在，并且也以许多你们不感知的其它方式存在：在一个与你们不同的次元里可能显出为一个自然的事件（译注：好比说风或雨）、梦的影像，甚至自己会推进的能量。能量绝对不会失去，那么，在你自己思想里的能量当你想完了它们以后并不会耗散，它们的能量在其它的世界里有其实相。", "en": "The kind of reality thus created by that portion of your consciousness forms a given kind of experience. It is valid and real. When you want to travel, you do so within the dimensions of the reality thus created. If you drive or fly from one city to another, you do not consider the journey imaginary. You are exploring the dimensions given. (10:18.) Now: If you alter that picture a little so that the images are somewhat scrambled — and you do this by altering the focus of your consciousness — then the familiar coordination is gone. Objects may appear blurred, ordinary sounds distorted. It seems as if you are on the outskirts of your own reality. In such a state, however, it is easy to see that your usual orientation may be but one of many frames of reference. (Pause.) If you did change the focus of your consciousness still further, you might then “bring in” another picture entirely. On the outside this would give you another reality. (Intently:) In it your “old” reality might still be somewhat perceivable as a ghost image,6 if you knew what to look for and remembered your former coordinates. On the inside, however, you would be traveling not around or about, but through one portion of the psyche with its reality, into another portion of the psyche with its reality. That kind of journey would not be any more imaginary than a trip from one city to another.", "source": "未知的实相卷二 · 第713节", "year": "1974–75", "tag": null, "short": "未知的实相卷二", "session": "713", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-037-e2822", "zh": "在一方面来说，你们发展了的单线式意识可以与你们对任何一种语言的应用相比拟。经验被设定了，非常的专门化了，而达成了一种看起来很紧密的组织，只因为（热切的）它局限了这么多实相。以那种说法，如果你会说两种语言，那就多少好一些，因为你的思绪有两条路可以选择。生物上来说，你在肉体上能够说现在在地球表面用到的任何语言。如果你学会许多语言，你会把它认为是一种成就。虽然这会涉及一些训练，但你会把它视为当然，却不会觉得它是吓人或不自然的。同样的，你的单线式意识只是许多种“语言”之一。其它的是一样天生的，一样自然的，一样在生物上是可能的。", "en": "In a way, the one-line kind of consciousness that you have developed can be correlated with your use of any one language. Experience is programmed, highly specialized, and attains a seemingly tight organization only because (intently) it limits so much of reality. In those terms, if you are bilingual you are somewhat better off, for your thoughts have a choice of two paths. Biologically, you are physically capable of speaking any language now in use on the face of the earth. You would consider it an achievement if you learned to speak many languages. You would not find it frightening or unnatural, though you would take it for granted that some training was involved. In the same way, your one-line kind of consciousness is but one of many “languages.” The others are as native, as natural, as biologically feasible. (11:18.) Ruburt has been involved with what he calls the Sumari language (as referred to in the notes at break). This is an expression of the consciousness at a different focus. It is the native expression of a kind of experience that happens just outside of your official one-line focus of consciousness. First of all, it breaks up verbal patterning.9 It is composed, however, of sounds and syllables Ruburt has heard before, made up of jumbled Romance languages.10 These are “foreign” as far as he is concerned. At the same time those sounds are, in your terms, filled with the implications of antiquity, and bring up connotations of the species’ and of the psyche’s past.", "source": "未知的实相卷二 · 第723节", "year": "1974–75", "tag": null, "short": "未知的实相卷二", "session": "723", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-037-e3047", "zh": "你开始质疑时间本质的本身时，那么，宇宙的“何时”就变得不重要了。宇宙的运动及能量仍然在由内而来。我当然明白那几乎很难说是一个科学性的声明——但“一切万有”一旦想到了一个物质的系统，它就被看不见的创造了，被赋予了创造力而一定会浮现成物质实相。", "en": "[However, as] you begin to question the nature of time itself, then the “when” of the universe is beside the point. The motion and energy of the universe still comes from within. I certainly realize that this is hardly a scientific statement — yet the moment that All That Is conceived of a physical system it was invisibly created, endowed with creativity, and bound to emerge [into physical reality].", "source": "未知的实相卷二 · 第744节", "year": "1974–75", "tag": null, "short": "未知的实相卷二", "session": "744", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-037-e3185", "zh": "这些心智全都共同合作，使你借着脑子的物理结构而活动（These minds all work together to keep you alive through the physical structure of the brain.）。当你用到所有这些心智，那时，只有那时，你对你的周围环境才变的完全地知觉：你会比现在更清楚地感知实相，更敏锐、更璀璨、也更确切。不过，在同时，你直接的理解它。你理解它的本质，而非你对它的实相的感知。对于你其它的心智天生具有的其它意识状态，你也会接受为自己的。你达成了真正的个人性。", "en": "These minds all work together to keep you alive through the physical structure of the brain. When you use all of these minds, then and only then do you become fully aware of your surroundings: You perceive reality more clearly than you do now, more sharply, brilliantly, and concisely. At the same time, however, you comprehend it directly. You comprehend what it is apart from your physical perception of it. You accept as yourself those other states of consciousness native to your other minds. You achieve true personhood.", "source": "心灵的本质 · 第763节", "year": "1975–77", "tag": null, "short": "心灵的本质", "session": "763", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-037-e3281", "zh": "因此，你们的心理实相暗含在我自己的实相之内，而我的在你们的之内。就如你们的实相暗含在威立二号（我们的猫）的实相之内——而它的在你们的之内。", "en": "Your kind of psychological reality is therefore implied in my own, and mine in yours, even as your kind of reality is implied in that of Willy Two (our kitten) — and his in yours.", "source": "心灵的本质 · 第790节", "year": "1975–77", "tag": null, "short": "心灵的本质", "session": "790", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-037-e3422", "zh": "我说内我会推理，但其推理并不受限于因与果之限制。内我在“架构二”的较广范围内之行动，解释了许多在你们世界里本来仿佛不合理的事件及看起来的巧合。在“架构二”之内的许多实相，无法适当的在“架构一”里向你解释为事实，只因为它们涉及了无法被转译为如你所认为的事实之心理厚度。反之，这些常常以艺术的象征语言出现，而你们许多的梦都是一种转译，在其中，“架构二”的事件以象征形式出现。", "en": "I said that the inner ego reasons, but its reasoning is not restricted to the cause-and-effect limitations that you apply to the reasoning process. The action of the inner ego within the wider sphere of Framework 2 explains many events and seeming coincidences that otherwise seem to make no sense within your world. Many realities within Framework 2 cannot suitably be explained as facts to you in Framework 1, simply because they involve psychological thicknesses that cannot be translated into facts as you think of them. These often appear in the symbolic language of the arts instead, and many of your dreams are translations in which the events of Framework 2 appear in symbolic form.", "source": "个人与群体事件的本质 · 第823节", "year": "1977–79", "tag": null, "short": "个人与群体事件的本质", "session": "823", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-037-e3447", "zh": "那么，有一些事件的“身体”，那是你会以某种方式具体化的，这几乎就像是你由胎儿的结构具体化出你自己的成人身体一样。以那种说法，身体处理物质的东西，虽然这些东西有它们自己的意识与实相。", "en": "There are bodies of events, then, that in a certain fashion you will materialize almost in the same way that you will materialize your own adult body from the structure of the fetus. In those terms the body works with physical properties — though again these properties, as discussed often, have their own consciousnesses and realities.", "source": "个人与群体事件的本质 · 第827节", "year": "1977–79", "tag": null, "short": "个人与群体事件的本质", "session": "827", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B07", "title": "实相到底是什么，又怎么被感知", "note": "心理时间最靠近赛斯存在的「气候」，它对实相的体验比言语更能告诉你一切存在的基本实相。自我既健康又有力，但学习在物质环境里好好运作的同时，也能在内在实相之内操纵。自己并不局限在自我的感知里，即使在梦或其他状态里，它仍存在于物质实相。类星体代表纯粹的能量，而反物质、正物质都是你们容易理解的实相。一个强烈的愿望会变成实相，而运作的规则不管你懂不懂都适用。透过探索内在实相，你确实与一切万有保持联系。人格死后体验了新的实相，不再是过去那个人，却包含了过去的一切还有更多。攻击性和破坏性的能量被无意识地向外投射时，会被赋予一种假的实相和暂时的物质有效性。一个清晰有力的意识需要经常休息才能正确诠释实相，否则它会扭曲所知觉的东西；而「艺术形式」常常是实相本质的象征性表现，会依感知者的能力被给予不同诠释。赛斯自己宣称：在另一个存在的层面，他有一个独立的实相。", "src": "第 48、168、219、249、281、304、310、422、533、547、881 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 48 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 168 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 219 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 249 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 281 节"}, {"n": 6, "id": null, "label": "第 304 节"}, {"n": 7, "id": null, "label": "第 310 节"}, {"n": 8, "id": null, "label": "第 422 节"}, {"n": 9, "id": null, "label": "第 533 节"}, {"n": 10, "id": null, "label": "第 547 节"}, {"n": 11, "id": null, "label": "第 881 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-037-e0106", "zh": "心理时间，我常说，非常接近我的存在所处的气候，你也存在其中，只不过是无意识。心理时间的体验，随着你对它持续不断的熟悉，将会告诉你们一切存在的基本实相，比言语能够告诉你们的还要多。", "en": "Psychological time, as I have said often, comes extremely close to the climate in which I have my existence, and which you exist in, but unconsciously. Experience with psychological time, and a continuous familiarity with it, will tell you more than words can about the basic realities of all existence.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第48节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "48", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-037-e0489", "zh": "他的自我的确很健康，且精力充足，但带有固执的倾向。不过就我们的目的来说，这样其实反而非常好，因为他正学习如何在物质环境中好好有效运作，同时又可以在内在实相之内操纵。", "en": "His ego is indeed a healthy and vigorous one, but of a stubborn bent. For our purposes however this is actually excellent, for he is learning effectively to operate well in the physical environment while at the same time he is manipulating within that inner reality.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第168节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "168", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-037-e0662", "zh": "但自己A并不局限在自我的感知里，因此可以说，自己A的感知并不完全的局限在他所存在的领域。在梦或其他的状态里就没有如此的局限了，当意识还在这些其他的状况时，自己A也仍存在于物质实相里。", "en": "But self A is not limited to the egos perceptions only, therefore it may be said that self As perceptions are not limited, in toto, to the field in which it exists. For it is not so limited in dreams and in other states, yet while consciousness is in these other conditions, self A still exists within physical reality.", "source": "早期课第5册 · 第219节", "year": "1966", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第5册", "session": "219", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-037-e0726", "zh": "基本上，类星体代表纯粹的能量。对于这意味着什么，你们的科学家目前不太有概念，因为相对来说，他们是以单一维度的角度来设想能量。你知道反物质是什么。你知道正物质是什么。这两者代表了你很容易了解的实相。", "en": "Now the quasars represent pure energy, basically speaking. Your scientists presently have little idea of what this means, for comparatively speaking they conceive of energy in one-dimensional terms. You know what antimatter is. You know what positive matter is. Both of these represent realities that you can understand rather easily.", "source": "早期课第6册 · 第249节", "year": "1967", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第6册", "session": "249", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-037-e0846", "zh": "意识心与这件事一点关系都没有。他非常希望这位朋友在场。这个希望变成实相。你必须了解运作的规则。因为不管你了不了解它们，也不管你真的想要实现的希望是不是这一个，规则都适用。", "en": "The conscious mind had nothing to do with this. He strongly wished for the friend’s presence. The wish became reality. You must understand the rules that apply. For they apply whether or not you understand them, and whether or not the wish is one that you really want fulfilled.", "source": "早期课第7册 · 第281节", "year": "1968", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第7册", "session": "281", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-037-e0899", "zh": "透过探索内在实相，你确实与一切万有保持联系。然而就你而言，基本上这个经验一定是独自的体会。你们两人以为自己维持着相对的孤立，这样想是正确的。具体来说，你们现在不应该加入那种计划中的社群。", "en": "Through exploring inner reality you are indeed in contact with All That Is. The experience must be primarily a solitary one however on your part. You are both correct in assuming that you maintain your relative isolation. Specifically you should not now join a community of the sort that is being planned.", "source": "早期课第7册 · 第304节", "year": "1968", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第7册", "session": "304", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-037-e0935", "zh": "现在所是的它们，可以说，也存在，而且与过去所是的它们截然不同。人格自从死后已经体验了新的实相，再也不完全是过去那个人了。然而，过去那个人以一种心理单位的形式存在着。现在所是的这个人、这个死后犹存的人，除了包含了它过去的一切，还有更多。", "en": "What they are now, so to speak, also exists, and as something distinct and different from what they were. The personality has experienced new realities since death, and is no longer precisely the person that was. The person that was exists as a sort of psychological unit, however. The person, the survival person that is, contains all that he was, and more.", "source": "早期课第7册 · 第310节", "year": "1968", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第7册", "session": "310", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-037-e1154", "zh": "至于你们的约克海滩形象。在这里，攻击性与破坏性的能量被无意识地向外投射，被给予一个假的实相和暂时的物质有效性。你们自己方面则有蛋白质的损失。", "en": "Now, as to your York Beach images. Here aggressive and destructive energies were unconsciously projected outward, given a pseudo reality and a temporary physical validity. There was a protein loss on your own parts.", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第422节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "422", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-037-e1588", "zh": "一个清楚、不杂乱、聪明而有力的意识需要有经常的休息时间，如果要维持它的效率，如果要它正确地诠释实相的话。不然它会扭曲它所知觉的东西。", "en": "A clear, uncluttered, bright, and powerful consciousness needs frequent rest periods if its efficiency is to be maintained, and if it is to correctly interpret reality. Otherwise it distorts what is perceived.", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第533节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "533", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-037-e1660", "zh": "这些“艺术形式”常常是实相本质的象征性表现。依照觉知到它的人的能力，它们会被给予不同的诠释。", "en": "Now: These “art forms” are often symbolic representations of the nature of reality. They will be interpreted in various ways, according to the abilities of those who perceive them.", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第547节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "547", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-037-e3525", "zh": "如我大半的读者所知，我并不宣称我现在是一个具有肉体的人。（停顿。）但我的确宣称，在另一个存在的层面，我有个独立的实相。我的身份来源看似奇怪，只因你们对自己的来源了解得这么少。今晚我开始这本书，我已给过书名，而珍•罗伯兹（在十二天前）已能感知部分将被包括在此的某些话题。不过，到现在为止，具体的东西只有罗勃•伯兹写下我说的这些话的纸张。", "en": "As most of my readers know, I make no claims of now having a physical personhood. (Pause.) I do claim an independent reality at another level of existence. My status and origins seem strange only because you have understood so little about your own origins. I am beginning this book this evening. I have already given the title, and at another level of consciousness Jane Roberts was able (12 days ago, for example) to perceive some glimpses of some of the subject matter that will be included here. So far, however, physically there is only the page of paper upon which Robert Butts is writing down these words I speak.", "source": "梦、进化与价值完成 · 第881节", "year": "1979–82", "tag": null, "short": "梦、进化与价值完成", "session": "881", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B08", "title": "实相与群体、文化、信念", "note": "实相不是纯私人的，它也发生在群体层面。你和这个实相的牵绊若太深、太急、学得不够，就可能回来得太快；死后你会认清自己曾扮演过的角色，并为下一世作计划，也可以先进入别的世界再回来。在更广的术语里没有因与果，虽然在你们的实相里这些是根本假设；某个信念把世界当成心智的事、把身体当成载体，于是感官被放进更宽的体验里。一个人的欲望会吸引相似的欲望，在另一个活动层面上重新发动旧冲突——这些反应其实都在同时发生。你的冲动如何影响未来经验、并形成群体实相的实际世界，是赛斯关心的题目。有「事件的身体」会被具体化，就像你从胎儿结构具体化出成人身体；而身体处理的那些物质属性，本身也有自己的意识和实相。连梦里的树都会渐渐变得有知觉、转而关注物质实相，直到梦的种子带来实质的树。身体是一个开放系统，不断对内里的实相和外在的刺激反应。在异教时代没有精神分裂症，因为那时的信念系统不支持那种诠释——行为符合当时实相的心理画面，而那些行为模式是人类传承的一部分。", "src": "第 483、562、535、636、645、694、857、887、906、921 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 483 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 562 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 535 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 636 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 645 节"}, {"n": 6, "id": null, "label": "第 694 节"}, {"n": 7, "id": null, "label": "第 857 节"}, {"n": 8, "id": null, "label": "第 887 节"}, {"n": 9, "id": null, "label": "第 906 节"}, {"n": 10, "id": null, "label": "第 921 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-037-e1319", "zh": "是你们自己。若你们非常疲惫，你们就休息。若你们明智，你们会花时间消化你们的知识，甚至筹划你们的下一世——你看，就像作家筹划他的下一本书。若你们与这个实相的牵绊太多，若你们太急不可耐，若你们学得还不够，你们就可能回来得太快。", "en": "you. If you are very tired, then you rest. If you are wise, you take time to digest your knowledge and to plan your next life even, you see, as a writer plans his next book. If you have too many ties with this reality and if you are too impatient, and if you have not learned sufficiently, then you may return too quickly.", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第483节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "483", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-037-e1732", "zh": "地球对他们来说是传说中的老家。他们形成了新的种族和人类，在身体上已不能适应你们的大气状况。不过，只要他们一天居住于物质的实相，他们便还在轮回中。可是，这些人中有一部分发生了突变而早已离开轮回了。", "en": "(Pause at 9:22.) Earth to them now is the legendary home. They formed new races and species that could no longer physically accommodate themselves to your atmospheric conditions. However, they also continued on the reincarnational level as long as they inhabited physical reality. Some of these have mutated and have long left the reincarnational cycle, however.", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第562节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "562", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-037-e1952", "zh": "那时候你一下子会知道很多事情，很广也很深。由了解到自己是什么，进而了解到自己曾经在过去当中扮演过什么角色，同时也开始为自己的下一世物质世界作生存计划——如果你打算再走一趟的话；同样的你也可以选择先进入别的世界，以后再回到物质世界。", "en": "You become aware, then, of an expanded awareness. What you are begins to include what you have been in other lives, and you begin to make plans for your next physical existence, if you decide upon one. You can instead enter another level of reality, and then return to a physical existence if you choose.", "source": "时空之外 · 第535节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "时空之外", "session": "535", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-037-e2118", "zh": "更广义地说，也并没有因与果，虽然在你们的实相里，这些是基本的假设②。", "en": "In larger terms there is no cause and effect either, though these are root assumptions in your reality.*", "source": "个人实相的本质 · 第636节", "year": "1972–73", "tag": null, "short": "个人实相的本质", "session": "636", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-037-e2170", "zh": "原先的信念意思是，他从精神的角度看待世界，大致是认为作家和意念是同一件事，把身体当成一个载体，而不认为它是活生生的有机体，但是生物属性的经验必须透过肉体而来，因此今晚感官被容许了自由，但这个经验是被他的心灵敏感度放大的。", "en": "The original belief meant that he considered his reality in mental terms, generally identifying a writer with ideas, and using his body as a vehicle rather than thinking of it as the living organism through which creaturehood experience must come. So this evening the senses were allowed their freedom, but the experience was magnified by his psychic sensitivity.", "source": "个人实相的本质 · 第645节", "year": "1972–73", "tag": null, "short": "个人实相的本质", "session": "645", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-037-e2481", "zh": "约瑟一时想要那房子的那个部分立即吸引了约瑟母亲那方一直有的同样欲望。在非物质的另一个活动层面上，这重新发动了在他们之间的老冲突。有那么一会儿，他们的欲望联合了他们，不过，现在的史黛拉比较能够了解她儿子的反应，透过他在这实相里的决定，她终于开始看到一眼他过去行为的理由，那在以前对她而言是无法理解的。", "en": "The portion that momentarily desired the house immediately attracted the same kind of desire always felt on the part of Joseph’s mother. This, on another level of activity than physical, reactivated old conflicts between them. For a while their desires united them. Now, however, Stella Butts is better able to understand her son’s reactions. Through his decision in this reality, she is finally beginning to glimpse the reasons for his actions in the past, that before were incomprehensible to her. Try to understand that all of these reactions are really happening at once … Joseph’s desire at this end attracted his mother’s like desire. (Pause.) In your terms, however, the reactions continue.", "source": "未知的实相卷一 · 第694节", "year": "1974–75", "tag": null, "short": "未知的实相卷一", "session": "694", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-037-e3499", "zh": "你的冲动如何影响你未来的经验，并且形成群体实相之实际世界？", "en": "How do your impulses affect your future experience, and help form the practical world of mass reality?", "source": "个人与群体事件的本质 · 第857节", "year": "1977–79", "tag": null, "short": "个人与群体事件的本质", "session": "857", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-037-e3555", "zh": "在一开始，也有其它不同的物种：“人－动物”及“动物－人”的组合，及许多其它的混种：以你们的说法，有些还持续了相当长的一段时间。这适用于所有的范围。有梦的树木，长着梦的树叶，它们逐渐的在那梦中有了知觉（带着温和的强调），转成实质，越来越关注于物质实相，直到它们的梦之种子最后带来了实质的树木。", "en": "In the beginning there were also species of various other kinds: combinations of man-animal and animal-man, and many other “crossbreed” species, some of fairly long duration in your terms. This applies to all areas. There were dream trees, with dream foliage, that gradually became aware within that dream (with gentle emphasis), turning physical, focusing more and more in physical reality, until their dream seeds finally brought forth physical trees.", "source": "梦、进化与价值完成 · 第887节", "year": "1979–82", "tag": null, "short": "梦、进化与价值完成", "session": "887", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-037-e3615", "zh": "在都市里有很大的交通流量，而身体在一瞬间知道如何跳开一辆驶近的车子。在身体的内部环境里有大得多的交通流量。在你无法想象的那么短的时间内得做一些决定——一些几乎还没开始前就已结束的反应；当身体对其内在实相反应，并且对从外在环境来的所有刺激反应时，那些反应快到你无法感知它们。身体是一个开放的系统。虽然在你看来身体仿佛如此坚实。但在它和世界之间有经常的化学反应、电磁性的调整、平衡的改变及关系的变化——在身体及每个其他实质事件，从行星及日月的位置，到最小的砂粒的位置，到任何一个人的肠子里最小的微生物，它们之间的关系所发生的改变（热切的）。", "en": "There is great traffic flow in a city: A body knows how to leap out of the way in a moment’s time from an approaching car. In the interior physical environment there is far greater traffic flow. There are decisions made in periods of time so brief you cannot imagine them—reactions that are almost over before they begin, reactions so fast you cannot perceive them as the body responds to its inner reality, and to all the stimuli from the exterior environment. The body is an open system. As solid as it seems to you, there are constant chemical reactions between it and the world, electromagnetic adjustments, alterations of balance, changes of relationships—alterations that occur between the body and its relationship with every other physical event, from the position of the planets and moon and the sun, to the position of the smallest grain of sand, to the tiniest microbe in anyone’s intestine (intently).", "source": "梦、进化与价值完成 · 第906节", "year": "1979–82", "tag": null, "short": "梦、进化与价值完成", "session": "906", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-037-e3675", "zh": "在异教的时代并没有精神分裂症，因为那时的信念系统并不支持那种诠释。这并不意味着你们现在会称为精神分裂症的某些行为不会发生，而是指一般而言，这种行为符合实相的心理画面。那是因为与精神分裂症相连的许多行为模式，是“被扭曲及被贬低的”行为模式的残留物。那些模式是人类传承的一部分，并且呼应一度曾有精确社会意义，且有确定目的的那些活动与能力。", "en": "There were no schizophrenics in the time of the pagans, for the belief systems did not support that kind of interpretation. This does not mean that certain behavior did not occur that you would now call schizophrenic. It means that generally speaking such behavior fit within the psychological picture of reality. It [did so] because many of the behavior patterns associated, now, with schizophrenia, are “distorted and debased” remnants of behavior patterns that are part and parcel of man’s heritage, and that harken back to activities and abilities that at one time had precise social meaning, and served definite purposes.", "source": "梦、进化与价值完成 · 第921节", "year": "1979–82", "tag": null, "short": "梦、进化与价值完成", "session": "921", "only_en": false}]}]}], "reading": [], "books": [{"name": "早期课第3册", "count": 7}, {"name": "早期课第1册", "count": 6}, {"name": "早期课第2册", "count": 6}, {"name": "个人实相的本质", "count": 6}, {"name": "早期课第4册", "count": 5}, {"name": "早期课第6册", "count": 5}, {"name": "早期课第7册", "count": 5}, {"name": "早期课第5册", "count": 5}, {"name": "心灵的本质", "count": 5}, {"name": "灵魂永生", "count": 5}, {"name": "梦、进化与价值完成", "count": 5}, {"name": "早期课第8册", "count": 4}, {"name": "早期课第9册", "count": 4}, {"name": "未知的实相卷二", "count": 4}, {"name": "个人与群体事件的本质", "count": 4}, {"name": "未知的实相卷一", "count": 4}, {"name": "时空之外", "count": 3}], "span": [1963, 1979], "stats": {"blocks": 8, "quotes": 83, "reading": 0, "reading_tagged": 0, "tagged": 0, "only_en": 6}};
